# INERT FOR THE CANONICAL BUILD. Read this before trusting it.
#
# Docker resolves .dockerignore at the CONTEXT ROOT. The canonical build for this image
# is `docker build -f dis/services/dis-ui-server/Dockerfile -t dis-ui-server .` run from
# the MONOREPO ROOT, so the file Docker reads is /.dockerignore, not this one.
#
# The previous header claimed this file "covers BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore lookup".
# That is FALSE. BuildKit's per-Dockerfile lookup is for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`
# — here that would be `Dockerfile.dockerignore` in this directory. A bare `.dockerignore`
# beside the Dockerfile is never consulted.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY BOUNDS THE IMAGE: the Dockerfile's explicit COPYs, plus /.dockerignore
# for anything that rides inside a copied directory (tests/, scripts/, .env*). Add
# exclusions THERE, not here.
#
# This file is kept only for a hypothetical directory-context build, which nothing does.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
.env
.env.*
